    "result_text": "All tests green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I changed and why.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the derived `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New cohesive helper** (`mapper/MemberId.java`) \u2014 holds all the identifier logic in one small, low-complexity class:\n- `of(owner)` builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`: region from postcode (`Locality`), 2-digit fiscal year (`Fiscal`), the same SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-upper-hex `HASH8`, and a Luhn `CHK` over the digits of the preceding segments.\n- `region(memberId)` / `fiscalYear(memberId)` read those segments back out (ignoring any `-<n>` collision suffix), so downstream values reference the memberId.\n\n**Edits kept small and local:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` field/accessors to `memberId` (trivial getters/setters only).\n- `AssignOwnerMemberId` / `DeduplicateOwnerMemberId` (renamed from the `...CustomerCode` classes) \u2014 one-line delegation to `MemberId.of`, and collision handling now dedups the `memberId`. Wiring updated in `owners.POST.yml`.\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 dropped the `membershipNumber` mapping + method; `fiscalYear` and `ownerSegment` now derive from `MemberId`; `locality`/`timezone` simplified to the plain `Locality.of(city, postcode)` (they weren't required to reference the memberId). `memberId` auto-maps by name.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 logs `memberId` (and the structured event's key is now `memberId`).\n- `RespondWithOwner` \u2014 removed the `checkDigit` line and its now-unused `luhn` helper.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced `customerCode` with `memberId`, removed `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` (the DTO regenerates from this).\n- All four `db/*/schema.sql` \u2014 renamed the column `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`.\n\n**Structural-impact choices:** the identifier logic lives in one new small class rather than being grown inside the large `OwnerMapper`; each function I touched stays trivial (mostly one-line delegations), and I avoided adding branches to any existing method.\n\nThe observed result, e.g. `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` \u2014 `NSW` + `26` (FY26) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `3` (Luhn CHK).",
